//! # Bit order
//!
//! A `B00011111` row below is a *big-endian* 1bpp row: bit 7 is the leftmost
//! pixel. That is exactly what `u8g2_DrawHXBMP` expects (`u8g2_bitmap.c`:
//! `mask = 1; ... mask <<= 1`), so the `B...` icons are kept as binary literals
//! and the hex ones are copied as-is.
//!
//! The header stores one byte per ROW, not per 8 rows, so a `B...` icon of width
//! 8 and height 8 has 8 bytes, and `Bluetooth_Icon` (8 wide) has 9.
//! `Display::draw_xbmp` reads them row by row, which is what `u8g2_DrawHXBMP`
//! does for a 1-byte-per-row source.

